# Put joints in free drive (move them by hand, their weight carried by the
# gravity model), or take them out of it.
#
# An action for the same reason as SetServo: refusal is a real outcome (a joint
# with no torque, no free-drive parameters, or an actuator that takes neither a
# torque nor a PWM duty) and must not be mistaken for success.
#
# Leaving free drive does not hand the joint back to its controller at once.
# The joint holds where it was left until the controller commands that pose:
# a trajectory controller still commands where the joint was when free drive
# began, and following it would throw the joint back there. Re-sync the
# controller to the robot, as for enabling (actuo_ros.robot_interface does).

# Goal
bool enable                # true = into free drive, false = out of it
string[] joints            # empty = every joint
---
# Result
bool ok
string reason              # why it was refused, or what was done
JointServoState[] joints    # state at the moment the request settled
---
# Feedback
string stage
